Topic 21 – Packages
Objective: Package creation, imports, fully qualified names, cross-package access and package organization.
No.	Program	Requirement
01	Create a Package	Create a package called utilities and a class inside it.
02	Import a Class	Create a class in one package and import it into another package.
03	Import Multiple Classes	Create two classes in the same package and import them into another package.
04	Fully Qualified Name	Access a class from another package using its fully qualified class name without import.
05	Package with Methods	Create a package containing a calculator class and access its methods from another package.
06	Cross-Package Objects	Create a class in package pages and instantiate it from a class in package tests.
07	Package Access Restrictions	Create default-access members in one package and attempt to access them from another package.
08	Package and Inheritance	Create a parent class in one package and a child class in another package. Access inherited members.
09	Utility Package	Create a reusable package containing string utilities, number utilities and calculation utilities. Access them from a runner class.
10	QA Framework Package Structure	Create base, pages, tests and utilities packages and implement a simple login execution using classes across packages.



