Program 07. Package Access Restrictions
=======================================

Demonstrates that default (package-private) members cannot be accessed outside their own package.

File 1: internal/SecretData.java

package internal;

public class SecretData {
    String defaultToken = "XYZ-123"; // Default access (no modifier)

    void defaultMethod() {           // Default access (no modifier)
        System.out.println("Internal method executed.");
    }
}

File 2: external/Program07_AccessRestriction.java

package external;

import internal.SecretData;

public class Program07_AccessRestriction {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        SecretData data = new SecretData();

        // UNCOMMENTING THESE WILL CAUSE COMPILE ERRORS:
        // System.out.println(data.defaultToken); // Error: defaultToken is not public in SecretData
        // data.defaultMethod();                  // Error: defaultMethod() is not public in SecretData

        System.out.println("Default members cannot be accessed outside their package.");
    }
}


Program 08. Package and Inheritance
===================================

Demonstrates cross-package inheritance where a subclass accesses public and protected members of a parent class in another package.

File 1: core/BaseDriver.java

package core;

public class BaseDriver {
    public String browser = "Firefox";
    protected String driverVersion = "v132.0";
    String internalFlag = "DEBUG"; // Default access
}

File 2: suite/Program08_CrossPackageInheritance.java

package suite;

import core.BaseDriver;

public class Program08_CrossPackageInheritance extends BaseDriver {
    public void displayDriverInfo() {
        System.out.println("Browser : " + browser);       // Accessible (public)
        System.out.println("Version : " + driverVersion); // Accessible (protected via inheritance)
        // System.out.println(internalFlag);              // COMPILE ERROR (default is package-private)
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Program08_CrossPackageInheritance test = new Program08_CrossPackageInheritance();
        test.displayDriverInfo();
    }
}


Program 09. Utility Package
===========================

Creates a multi-class reusable package utils and accesses all three utility classes from a runner class.

File 1: utils/StringUtils.java

package utils;

public class StringUtils {
    public static String toUpper(String text) {
        return text.toUpperCase();
    }
}

File 2: utils/NumberUtils.java

package utils;

public class NumberUtils {
    public static boolean isEven(int num) {
        return num % 2 == 0;
    }
}

File 3: utils/CalcUtils.java

package utils;

public class CalcUtils {
    public static double calculateDiscount(double price, double percent) {
        return price - (price * percent / 100);
    }
}

File 4: mainapp/Program09_UtilityRunner.java

package mainapp;

import utils.StringUtils;
import utils.NumberUtils;
import utils.CalcUtils;

public class Program09_UtilityRunner {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println("Uppercase : " + StringUtils.toUpper("automation"));
        System.out.println("Is 42 Even: " + NumberUtils.isEven(42));
        System.out.println("Final Price: ₹" + CalcUtils.calculateDiscount(1000, 15));
    }
}

Program 10. QA Framework Package Structure
==========================================

Implements a miniature Page Object Model (POM) login flow distributed across base, utilities, pages, and tests.

File 1: base/BaseTest.java

package base;

public class BaseTest {
    protected void openBrowser(String url) {
        System.out.println("[Base] Launching browser and navigating to: " + url);
    }

    protected void closeBrowser() {
        System.out.println("[Base] Closing browser session.");
    }
}

File 2: utilities/WaitUtil.java

package utilities;

public class WaitUtil {
    public static void waitForElement(String elementName) {
        System.out.println("[Utility] Waiting for element to be visible: " + elementName);
    }
}

File 3: pages/LoginPage.java

package pages;

import utilities.WaitUtil;

public class LoginPage {
    public void enterUsername(String user) {
        WaitUtil.waitForElement("Username Field");
        System.out.println("[Page] Entering username: " + user);
    }

    public void enterPassword(String pass) {
        WaitUtil.waitForElement("Password Field");
        System.out.println("[Page] Entering password: ********");
    }

    public void clickLogin() {
        System.out.println("[Page] Clicking Login button.");
    }
}

File 4: tests/Program10_LoginTest.java

package tests;

import base.BaseTest;
import pages.LoginPage;

public class Program10_LoginTest extends BaseTest {
    public void executeLoginTest() {
        openBrowser("https://example.com");

        LoginPage loginPage = new LoginPage();
        loginPage.enterUsername("testuser@example.com");
        loginPage.enterPassword("Pass@123");
        loginPage.clickLogin();

        System.out.println("[Test] Assertion Passed: User landed on Dashboard.");
        closeBrowser();
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Program10_LoginTest test = new Program10_LoginTest();
        test.executeLoginTest();
    }
}


